Package: privux-cli
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}
Recommends: apparmor, network-manager, nftables, systemd-resolved, unattended-upgrades
Description: Privacy hardening tool for Privux
 The privux command applies and checks the privacy configuration of the system:
 inbound firewall, encrypted DNS, per-network MAC addresses, kernel and network
 hardening, Firefox policies and automatic security updates.
 .
 Every setting is an independent option with its own default. The graphical
 settings panel is a thin layer over this command.

Package: privux-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 apparmor,
 firefox-esr,
 flatpak,
 kde-plasma-desktop,
 libreoffice,
 network-manager,
 nftables,
 plasma-discover-backend-flatpak,
 privux-cli (= ${binary:Version}),
 systemd-resolved,
 thunderbird,
 unattended-upgrades,
Recommends:
 amd64-microcode,
 btrfs-progs,
 firmware-atheros,
 firmware-iwlwifi,
 firmware-linux,
 firmware-realtek,
 intel-microcode,
 snapper,
Description: Privux desktop (KDE Plasma with high-privacy defaults)
 Meta-package that installs the Privux desktop: KDE Plasma, Firefox ESR,
 LibreOffice, Thunderbird and the privux hardening tool.
 .
 The firmware and microcode packages come from the non-free-firmware
 component. They are the only closed-source part of the system and are needed
 for Wi-Fi to work and for CPU security fixes.
